# Settings for the dashboard/API container (copy to api.env), the ones the systemd install keeps in
# /etc/moreopenrepeater/env, for example:
# MOREOPENREPEATER_ADMIN_USER=admin
# MOREOPENREPEATER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
# The AllStar link service and the SIP trunk page talk to the node's management interface (AMI) from this
# container, so give it the same settings the core has. With the node as a container
# (docker compose --profile allstar ...) it is `allstar` on the private network, and the secret is MOR_AMI_SECRET
# from allstar.env. (With the old host layout, compose.host-network.yaml, a host Asterisk is at 127.0.0.1.)
# MOREOPENREPEATER_AMI_HOST=allstar
# MOREOPENREPEATER_AMI_PORT=5038
# MOREOPENREPEATER_AMI_USER=admin
# MOREOPENREPEATER_AMI_SECRET=
# The node's number, if it should not be read from the node's own setup.
# MOREOPENREPEATER_AMI_NODE=
# The dashboard's port is set in .env (MOR_API_PORT), not here: inside the container it is always 8000.
